  "quikchat-backend/Dockerfile": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/Dockerfile`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the steps to build a multi-stage Docker image for the QuikChat backend application, resulting in a small, production-ready image.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - This is a Dockerfile and does not contain code definitions.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Multi-stage Build: Uses a `golang:1.21-alpine` image for building and an `alpine:latest` image for the final runtime, reducing image size.\n  - Dependency Caching: Downloads Go modules in a separate step to leverage Docker layer caching.\n  - Static Compilation: `CGO_ENABLED=0` ensures a statically linked binary.\n  - Port Exposure: Exposes port 8080 for the application.\n  - Command: Sets the default command to run the compiled `quikchat` binary.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/README.md": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/README.md`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides an overview, architectural details, and instructions for setting up and running the QuikChat backend locally.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - This is a documentation file and does not contain code definitions.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Documentation: Describes the project's language, architecture, database, cache, API type, and local setup steps using Docker Compose.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/api/swagger.yaml": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/api/swagger.yaml`\n- High-Level Purpose: A placeholder file for the OpenAPI (Swagger) specification of the QuikChat API.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - This is a specification file and currently contains minimal placeholder information for the API title, version, and description. It does not define any actual API paths yet.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/cmd/api/main.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/cmd/api/main.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: The main entry point for the QuikChat backend application, responsible for initializing all components, setting up dependency injection, starting the HTTP server, and handling graceful shutdown.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `main()`: The application's entry point. It loads configuration, connects to the database, initializes the WebSocket hub, creates repository, external service, and use case (service) implementations, sets up HTTP handlers and the router, and starts the HTTP server with graceful shutdown.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Application Bootstrap: Orchestrates the startup sequence of the entire backend.\n  - Dependency Injection: Manually wires up all dependencies (repositories, services, handlers) at startup.\n  - Graceful Shutdown: Implements signal handling (`SIGINT`, `SIGTERM`) to allow the HTTP server to shut down cleanly within a timeout.\n  - Logging: Initializes and uses `slog` for structured logging.\n  - Database Connection: Establishes a connection pool to PostgreSQL.\n  - WebSocket Hub: Starts the WebSocket hub in a goroutine.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/docker-compose.yml": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/docker-compose.yml`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines and configures a multi-container Docker application for the QuikChat backend, including the Go application, a PostgreSQL database, and a Redis instance.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Services**:\n    - `backend`: The Go application service, built from the `Dockerfile`, exposed on port 8080, depends on `db` and `redis`, and mounts the local directory.\n    - `db`: A PostgreSQL 15-alpine database service, exposed on port 5432, with persistent data volume and health checks.\n    - `redis`: A Redis 7-alpine service, exposed on port 6379, with persistent data volume and health checks.\n  - **Volumes**:\n    - `postgres_data`: A named volume for PostgreSQL data persistence.\n    - `redis_data`: A named volume for Redis data persistence.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Docker Compose: Orchestrates multiple Docker containers.\n  - Service Health Checks: Ensures dependent services are ready before starting.\n  - Volume Mounting: Persists data for the database and Redis.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/go.mod": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/go.mod`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the Go module for the QuikChat backend, specifying its module path, Go version, and direct dependencies.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - This is a Go module definition file and does not contain code definitions.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Go Module: Declares `quikchat` as the module.\n  - Dependencies: Lists direct dependencies like `github.com/go-chi/chi/v5`, `github.com/golang-jwt/jwt/v5`, `github.com/google/uuid`, `github.com/gorilla/websocket`, `github.com/jackc/pgx/v5`, `github.com/joho/godotenv`, and `golang.org/x/crypto`.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/external/s3/s3.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/external/s3/s3.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines an interface for S3-compatible object storage operations and provides a mock implementation for development.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Interfaces**:\n    - `S3Client`: Interface for S3 interactions.\n      - Methods: `GeneratePresignedUploadURL(ctx context.Context, bucket, key string, expiry time.Duration) (string, error)`, `GeneratePresignedDownloadURL(ctx context.Context, bucket, key string, expiry time.Duration) (string, error)`.\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `MockS3Client`: A placeholder implementation of `S3Client`.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewMockS3Client() S3Client`: Public constructor for `MockS3Client`.\n    - `GeneratePresignedUploadURL(ctx context.Context, bucket, key string, expiry time.Duration) (string, error)`: Public method of `MockS3Client` that returns a fake upload URL.\n    - `GeneratePresignedDownloadURL(ctx context.Context, bucket, key string, expiry time.Duration) (string, error)`: Public method of `MockS3Client` that returns a fake download URL.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Interface-based Design: Defines a contract for S3 operations, allowing for different implementations (e.g., real AWS S3, mock).\n  - Mock Implementation: Provides a simple, non-functional implementation useful for testing and local development without actual S3 credentials.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/handler/http/handler/friend_handler.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/handler/http/handler/friend_handler.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements HTTP handlers for friend-related API endpoints, translating incoming HTTP requests into calls to the `FriendUseCase` and formatting HTTP responses.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `FriendHandler`: Holds a reference to the `FriendUseCase` for business logic execution.\n      - Fields: `friendService` (usecase.FriendUseCase).\n    - `SendFriendRequest`: Request body structure for sending a friend request.\n      - Fields: `Username` (string).\n    - `RespondToRequest`: Request body structure for responding to a friend request.\n      - Fields: `Action` (string, e.g., \"accept\", \"decline\").\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewFriendHandler(friendService usecase.FriendUseCase) *FriendHandler`: Public constructor for `FriendHandler`.\n    - `SendRequest(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public HTTP handler for sending a friend request.\n    - `ListIncomingRequests(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public HTTP handler for listing incoming friend requests.\n    - `RespondToRequest(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public HTTP handler for responding to a specific friend request.\n    - `ListFriends(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public HTTP handler for listing the current user's friends.\n    - `Unfriend(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public HTTP handler for unfriending a user.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - HTTP Handler: Implements `http.HandlerFunc` pattern.\n  - Request/Response Marshalling: Uses `json.NewDecoder` and `json.NewEncoder` for JSON payload handling.\n  - Error Handling: Returns appropriate HTTP status codes and error messages.\n  - Context Usage: Extracts `user_id` from the request context, typically set by authentication middleware.\n  - URL Parameters: Uses `chi.URLParam` to extract parameters like `requestID` and `username` from the URL path.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/handler/http/handler/message_handler.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/handler/http/handler/message_handler.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements HTTP handlers for message-related API endpoints and a WebSocket endpoint for real-time communication.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Variables**:\n    - `upgrader`: Module-level `websocket.Upgrader` configured to allow all origins (for development).\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `MessageHandler`: Holds references to the `MessageUseCase` and the WebSocket `Hub`.\n      - Fields: `messageService` (usecase.MessageUseCase), `hub` (*ws.Hub).\n    - `SendMessageRequest`: Request body structure for sending a message.\n      - Fields: `Type` (domain.MessageType), `Content` (string).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewMessageHandler(messageService usecase.MessageUseCase, hub *ws.Hub) *MessageHandler`: Public constructor for `MessageHandler`.\n    - `SendMessage(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public HTTP handler to send a new message to a conversation.\n    - `GetMessages(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public HTTP handler to retrieve messages for a specific conversation, supporting cursor-based pagination.\n    - `GetPresignedURL(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public HTTP handler to generate a presigned URL for media uploads to S3.\n    - `ServeWs(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public HTTP handler to upgrade an HTTP connection to a WebSocket connection, registering the client with the hub.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - HTTP Handler: Implements `http.HandlerFunc` pattern for REST endpoints.\n  - WebSocket Endpoint: Handles WebSocket connection upgrades and client registration.\n  - Request/Response Marshalling: Uses `json.NewDecoder` and `json.NewEncoder` for JSON payload handling.\n  - Error Handling: Returns appropriate HTTP status codes and error messages.\n  - Context Usage: Extracts `user_id` from the request context.\n  - URL Parameters: Uses `chi.URLParam` to extract `conversationID`.\n  - Query Parameters: Uses `r.URL.Query().Get` for `cursor`, `limit`, and `filename`.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/handler/http/handler/user_handler.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/handler/http/handler/user_handler.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements HTTP handlers for user-related API endpoints, translating incoming HTTP requests into calls to the `UserUseCase` and formatting HTTP responses.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `UserHandler`: Holds a reference to the `UserUseCase` for business logic execution.\n      - Fields: `userService` (usecase.UserUseCase).\n    - `RegisterRequest`: Request body structure for user registration.\n      - Fields: `Username` (string), `Password` (string).\n    - `LoginRequest`: Request body structure for user login.\n      - Fields: `Username` (string), `Password` (string).\n    - `AuthResponse`: Response body structure for successful login, containing tokens.\n      - Fields: `AccessToken` (string), `RefreshToken` (string).\n    - `UpdateProfileRequest`: Request body structure for updating user profile.\n      - Fields: `DisplayName` (*string), `ProfileImageURL` (*string).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewUserHandler(userService usecase.UserUseCase) *UserHandler`: Public constructor for `UserHandler`.\n    - `Register(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public HTTP handler for user registration.\n    - `Login(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public HTTP handler for user login.\n    - `GetCurrentUser(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public HTTP handler to get the ID of the currently authenticated user.\n    - `GetProfileByUsername(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public HTTP handler to retrieve a user's profile by username.\n    - `UpdateProfile(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public HTTP handler to update the authenticated user's profile.\n    - `BlockUser(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public HTTP handler to block another user.\n    - `UnblockUser(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public HTTP handler to unblock another user.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - HTTP Handler: Implements `http.HandlerFunc` pattern.\n  - Request/Response Marshalling: Uses `json.NewDecoder` and `json.NewEncoder` for JSON payload handling.\n  - Error Handling: Returns appropriate HTTP status codes and error messages.\n  - Context Usage: Extracts `user_id` from the request context, typically set by authentication middleware.\n  - URL Parameters: Uses `chi.URLParam` to extract parameters from the URL path.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/handler/http/router/router.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/handler/http/router/router.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Configures the HTTP router for the QuikChat backend, defining all API endpoints, applying middleware, and serving static frontend files.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `New(userHandler *handler.UserHandler, friendHandler *handler.FriendHandler, messageHandler *handler.MessageHandler, hub *ws.Hub, jwtSecret string) http.Handler`: Public function that initializes and returns a new `chi.Mux` HTTP router with all defined routes and middleware.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Chi Router: Uses `github.com/go-chi/chi/v5` for routing.\n  - Middleware: Applies `chi_middleware.Recoverer` and `middleware.RequestLogger` globally. `middleware.Auth` is applied to protected routes.\n  - Static File Serving: Serves files from the `./web` directory (presumably the frontend build output).\n  - Route Grouping: Organizes routes into public (`/api/v1/auth`), protected (`/api/v1` with auth middleware), and WebSocket (`/api/v1/ws`) groups.\n  - Dependency Injection: Receives handler instances, the WebSocket hub, and JWT secret in its constructor.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/storage/postgres/block_repository.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/storage/postgres/block_repository.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements the `BlockRepository` interface, providing PostgreSQL-specific data access logic for user blocking.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `BlockRepository`: Implements `repository.BlockRepository`, holding a database connection pool.\n      - Fields: `db` (*pgxpool.Pool).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewBlockRepository(db *pgxpool.Pool) *BlockRepository`: Public constructor for `BlockRepository`.\n    - `Save(ctx context.Context, blockerID, blockedID int64) error`: Public method to record a user block, preventing duplicate entries with `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`.\n    - `Delete(ctx context.Context, blockerID, blockedID int64) error`: Public method to remove a user block.\n    - `IsBlocked(ctx context.Context, userID1, userID2 int64) (bool, error)`: Public method to check if two users have blocked each other in either direction.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Repository Pattern: Provides an abstraction layer over database operations.\n  - PostgreSQL Interaction: Uses `pgxpool` for database queries.\n  - `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`: Used in `Save` to gracefully handle attempts to block an already blocked user.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/storage/postgres/conversation_repository.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/storage/postgres/conversation_repository.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements the `ConversationRepository` interface, providing PostgreSQL-specific data access logic for conversations and participants.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `ConversationRepository`: Implements `repository.ConversationRepository`, holding a database connection pool.\n      - Fields: `db` (*pgxpool.Pool).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewConversationRepository(db *pgxpool.Pool) repository.ConversationRepository`: Public constructor for `ConversationRepository`.\n    - `Save(ctx context.Context, conversation *domain.Conversation) error`: Public method to insert a new conversation into the database.\n    - `AddParticipant(ctx context.Context, conversationID, userID int64) error`: Public method to add a user as a participant to a conversation, handling duplicates.\n    - `IsUserInConversation(ctx context.Context, userID, conversationID int64) (bool, error)`: Public method to check if a specific user is a participant in a given conversation.\n    - `FindParticipantIDs(ctx context.Context, conversationID int64) ([]int64, error)`: Public method to retrieve all user IDs participating in a conversation.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Repository Pattern: Provides an abstraction layer over database operations.\n  - PostgreSQL Interaction: Uses `pgxpool` for database queries.\n  - `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`: Used in `AddParticipant` to prevent duplicate entries.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/storage/postgres/friend_repository.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/storage/postgres/friend_repository.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements the `FriendRepository` interface, providing PostgreSQL-specific data access logic for friend requests and friendships.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `FriendRepository`: Implements `repository.FriendRepository`, holding a database connection pool.\n      - Fields: `db` (*pgxpool.Pool).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewFriendRepository(db *pgxpool.Pool) *FriendRepository`: Public constructor for `FriendRepository`.\n    - `SaveRequest(ctx context.Context, req *domain.FriendRequest) error`: Public method to insert a new friend request into the database.\n    - `FindRequestByID(ctx context.Context, requestID int64) (*domain.FriendRequest, error)`: Public method to retrieve a friend request by its ID.\n    - `FindRequestBySenderAndReceiver(ctx context.Context, senderID, receiverID int64) (*domain.FriendRequest, error)`: Public method to find an existing friend request between two specific users, regardless of sender/receiver roles.\n    - `UpdateRequestStatus(ctx context.Context, requestID int64, status domain.FriendRequestStatus) error`: Public method to update the status of a friend request.\n    - `FindPendingRequestsByReceiverID(ctx context.Context, userID int64) ([]*domain.FriendRequest, error)`: Public method to retrieve all pending friend requests for a given receiver.\n    - `FindFriendsByUserID(ctx context.Context, userID int64) ([]*domain.User, error)`: Public method to retrieve a list of `User` objects who are friends with the given user.\n    - `DeleteFriendship(ctx context.Context, userID1, userID2 int64) error`: Public method to delete an accepted friendship between two users.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Repository Pattern: Provides an abstraction layer over database operations.\n  - PostgreSQL Interaction: Uses `pgxpool` for database queries and transactions.\n  - Error Handling: Specifically handles `pgx.ErrNoRows` to return `nil` for not found entities.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/storage/postgres/message_repository.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/storage/postgres/message_repository.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements the `MessageRepository` interface, providing PostgreSQL-specific data access logic for message entities.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `MessageRepository`: Implements `repository.MessageRepository`, holding a database connection pool.\n      - Fields: `db` (*pgxpool.Pool).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewMessageRepository(db *pgxpool.Pool) repository.MessageRepository`: Public constructor for `MessageRepository`.\n    - `Save(ctx context.Context, message *domain.Message) error`: Public method to insert a new message into the database and retrieve its generated ID and creation timestamp.\n    - `FindMessagesByConversationID(ctx context.Context, conversationID int64, cursor int64, limit int) ([]*domain.Message, error)`: Public method to retrieve messages for a given conversation, supporting cursor-based pagination and joining with user data to populate sender information.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Repository Pattern: Provides an abstraction layer over database operations.\n  - PostgreSQL Interaction: Uses `pgxpool` for database queries.\n  - Cursor-based Pagination: Implements `WHERE m.id \u003c $2` and `ORDER BY m.id DESC` for efficient retrieval of older messages.\n  - Data Enrichment: Joins with the `users` table to include sender details in the returned `domain.Message` objects.\n  - Result Reversal: Reverses the order of fetched messages to return them in ascending order (oldest first) for chat display.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/storage/postgres/user_repository.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/storage/postgres/user_repository.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements the `UserRepository` interface, providing PostgreSQL-specific data access logic for user entities.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `UserRepository`: Implements `repository.UserRepository`, holding a database connection pool.\n      - Fields: `db` (*pgxpool.Pool).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewUserRepository(db *pgxpool.Pool) *UserRepository`: Public constructor for `UserRepository`.\n    - `Save(ctx context.Context, user *domain.User) error`: Public method to insert a new user into the database.\n    - `FindByUsername(ctx context.Context, username string) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method to retrieve a user by their username.\n    - `FindByID(ctx context.Context, id int64) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method to retrieve a user by their ID.\n    - `Update(ctx context.Context, user *domain.User) error`: Public method to update an existing user's profile information.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Repository Pattern: Provides an abstraction layer over database operations.\n  - PostgreSQL Interaction: Uses `pgxpool` for database queries.\n  - Error Handling: Specifically handles `pgx.ErrNoRows` to return `nil` for not found entities.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/ws/client.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/ws/client.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Represents a single WebSocket client connection and handles its read and write operations, including heartbeats.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `writeWait`: Duration for write deadlines.\n    - `pongWait`: Duration for read deadlines (pong timeout).\n    - `pingPeriod`: Interval for sending ping messages.\n    - `maxMessageSize`: Maximum allowed message size.\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `Client`: Represents an individual WebSocket client.\n      - Fields: `Hub` (*Hub), `Conn` (*websocket.Conn), `Send` (chan []byte), `UserID` (int64).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `ReadPump()`: Public method that continuously reads messages from the WebSocket connection and handles control frames (like pongs). It's primarily for maintaining the connection, as application messages are sent via HTTP.\n    - `WritePump()`: Public method that continuously writes messages from the `Send` channel to the WebSocket connection, and sends periodic ping messages.\n    - `send(data interface{})`: Internal method to marshal data to JSON and send it to the client's `Send` channel.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - WebSocket Client: Manages the lifecycle of a single WebSocket connection.\n  - Goroutines: `ReadPump` and `WritePump` are designed to run in separate goroutines.\n  - Heartbeat: Implements ping/pong mechanism to keep the connection alive and detect dead clients.\n  - Message Buffering: Uses a buffered channel (`Send`) for outgoing messages.\n  - Graceful Shutdown: Handles closing the connection and unregistering from the hub on errors or close.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/ws/hub.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/ws/hub.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Manages the lifecycle of WebSocket clients, including registration, unregistration, and broadcasting messages to specific users or groups of users.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `Hub`: Maintains the set of active WebSocket clients and channels for managing them.\n      - Fields: `clients` (map[*Client]bool), `register` (chan *Client), `unregister` (chan *Client), `userClients` (map[int64]map[*Client]bool), `mu` (sync.RWMutex).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewHub() *Hub`: Public constructor for `Hub`.\n    - `Run()`: Public method that runs the hub's main loop, processing client registration and unregistration requests.\n    - `Register() chan\u003c- *Client`: Public method that returns the channel for registering new clients.\n    - `Unregister() chan\u003c- *Client`: Public method that returns the channel for unregistering clients.\n    - `BroadcastToUsers(message *domain.Message, userIDs []int64)`: Public method to send a message to all connected WebSocket clients associated with a given list of user IDs.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - WebSocket Hub: Centralized component for managing multiple WebSocket connections.\n  - Concurrency: Uses channels (`register`, `unregister`) for safe client management and a `sync.RWMutex` for protecting shared client maps during broadcasts.\n  - Client Management: Keeps track of all active clients and maps user IDs to their connected clients (supporting multiple devices per user).\n  - Message Broadcasting: Sends messages to specific users by iterating through their associated clients.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/domain/conversation.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/domain/conversation.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the domain models for conversations and conversation participants in the QuikChat application.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Types**:\n    - `ConversationType`: String type representing the type of a conversation.\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `ConversationTypePrivate`: `ConversationType` enum value for private conversations.\n    - `ConversationTypeGroup`: `ConversationType` enum value for group conversations.\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `Conversation`: Represents a chat conversation.\n      - Fields: `ID` (int64), `Type` (ConversationType), `CreatedAt` (time.Time).\n    - `ConversationParticipant`: Represents a user's participation in a conversation.\n      - Fields: `ConversationID` (int64), `UserID` (int64), `JoinedAt` (time.Time).\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Domain Model: Defines core business entities for chat.\n  - JSON Tagging: Uses `json:\"...\"` tags for JSON serialization/deserialization.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/domain/friend.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/domain/friend.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the domain models for friend requests and established friendships within the QuikChat application.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `FriendRequestStatusPending`: `FriendRequestStatus` enum value for a pending request.\n    - `FriendRequestStatusAccepted`: `FriendRequestStatus` enum value for an accepted request.\n    - `FriendRequestStatusDeclined`: `FriendRequestStatus` enum value for a declined request.\n  - **Types**:\n    - `FriendRequestStatus`: String type representing the status of a friend request.\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `FriendRequest`: Represents a request from one user to another.\n      - Fields: `ID` (int64), `SenderID` (int64), `ReceiverID` (int64), `Status` (FriendRequestStatus), `CreatedAt` (time.Time), `UpdatedAt` (time.Time).\n    - `Friendship`: Represents an established friendship between two users.\n      - Fields: `UserID1` (int64), `UserID2` (int64), `CreatedAt` (time.Time).\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Domain Model: Defines core business entities.\n  - JSON Tagging: Uses `json:\"...\"` tags for JSON serialization/deserialization.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/domain/message.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/domain/message.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the `Message` domain entity structure and related types for the QuikChat application.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Types**:\n    - `MessageType`: String type representing the type of a message.\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `MessageTypeText`: `MessageType` enum value for text messages.\n    - `MessageTypeMedia`: `MessageType` enum value for media messages.\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `Message`: Represents a chat message.\n      - Fields: `ID` (int64), `ConversationID` (int64), `SenderID` (int64), `Type` (MessageType), `Content` (string), `CreatedAt` (time.Time), `Sender` (*User, optional).\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Domain Model: Defines a core business entity for chat.\n  - JSON Tagging: Uses `json:\"...\"` tags for JSON serialization/deserialization, including `omitempty` for optional fields.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/domain/user.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/domain/user.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the `User` domain entity structure, representing a user in the QuikChat application.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `User`: Represents a user entity with various attributes.\n      - Fields: `ID` (int64), `Username` (string), `PasswordHash` (string, marked to be ignored in JSON), `DisplayName` (string), `ProfileImageURL` (*string), `CreatedAt` (time.Time), `UpdatedAt` (time.Time), `LastSeenAt` (*time.Time).\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Domain Model: Represents a core business entity.\n  - JSON Tagging: Uses `json:\"...\"` tags for JSON serialization/deserialization, including `json:\"-\"` to hide sensitive fields.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/repository/block_repository.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/repository/block_repository.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the interface for data access operations related to user blocking.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Interfaces**:\n    - `BlockRepository`: Interface for user block data persistence.\n      - Methods: `Save(ctx context.Context, blockerID, blockedID int64) error`, `Delete(ctx context.Context, blockerID, blockedID int64) error`, `IsBlocked(ctx context.Context, userID1, userID2 int64) (bool, error)`.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/repository/conversation_repository.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/repository/conversation_repository.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the interface for data access operations related to conversations and their participants.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Interfaces**:\n    - `ConversationRepository`: Interface for conversation and participant data persistence.\n      - Methods: `Save(ctx context.Context, conversation *domain.Conversation) error`, `AddParticipant(ctx context.Context, conversationID, userID int64) error`, `IsUserInConversation(ctx context.Context, userID, conversationID int64) (bool, error)`, `FindParticipantIDs(ctx context.Context, conversationID int64) ([]int64, error)`.",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/repository/friend_repository.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/repository/friend_repository.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the interface for data access operations related to friend requests and friendships.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Interfaces**:\n    - `FriendRepository`: Interface for friend request and friendship data persistence.\n      - Methods: `SaveRequest(ctx context.Context, req *domain.FriendRequest) error`, `FindRequestByID(ctx context.Context, requestID int64) (*domain.FriendRequest, error)`, `FindRequestBySenderAndReceiver(ctx context.Context, senderID, receiverID int64) (*domain.FriendRequest, error)`, `UpdateRequestStatus(ctx context.Context, requestID int64, status domain.FriendRequestStatus) error`, `FindPendingRequestsByReceiverID(ctx context.Context, userID int64) ([]*domain.FriendRequest, error)`, `FindFriendsByUserID(ctx context.Context, userID int64) ([]*domain.User, error)`, `DeleteFriendship(ctx context.Context, userID1, userID2 int64) error`.",
