  "quikchat-backend/migrations/000001_create_users_table.up.sql": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/migrations/000001_create_users_table.up.sql`\n- High-Level Purpose: SQL script to create the initial `users` table and an index for the QuikChat backend database.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Database Tables**:\n    - `users`: Table to store user information.\n      - Fields: `id` (BIGSERIAL, PRIMARY KEY), `username` (VARCHAR(50), UNIQUE, NOT NULL), `password_hash` (VARCHAR(255), NOT NULL), `display_name` (VARCHAR(50), NOT NULL), `profile_image_url` (VARCHAR(255)), `created_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()), `updated_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()), `last_seen_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ).\n  - **Database Indexes**:\n    - `idx_users_username`: An index on the `username` column of the `users` table for efficient lookups.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/migrations/000002_create_friend_requests_table.up.sql": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/migrations/000002_create_friend_requests_table.up.sql`\n- High-Level Purpose: SQL script to create the `friend_requests` table, define a custom `friend_request_status` ENUM type, and add indexes for efficient querying.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Database Types**:\n    - `friend_request_status`: An ENUM type with values 'pending', 'accepted', 'declined'.\n  - **Database Tables**:\n    - `friend_requests`: Table to store friend request information.\n      - Fields: `id` (BIGSERIAL, PRIMARY KEY), `sender_id` (BIGINT, NOT NULL, REFERENCES `users`), `receiver_id` (BIGINT, NOT NULL, REFERENCES `users`), `status` (friend_request_status, NOT NULL, DEFAULT 'pending'), `created_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()), `updated_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()).\n  - **Database Constraints**:\n    - `UNIQUE(sender_id, receiver_id)`: Ensures that there can only be one pending/active request between any two users.\n  - **Database Indexes**:\n    - `idx_friend_requests_sender_id`: Index on `sender_id` for faster lookups of sent requests.\n    - `idx_friend_requests_receiver_id`: Index on `receiver_id` for faster lookups of received requests.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/migrations/000003_create_user_blocks_table.up.sql": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/migrations/000003_create_user_blocks_table.up.sql`\n- High-Level Purpose: SQL script to create the `user_blocks` table and an index for managing user blocking relationships.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Database Tables**:\n    - `user_blocks`: Table to store which user has blocked another user.\n      - Fields: `blocker_id` (BIGINT, NOT NULL, REFERENCES `users`), `blocked_id` (BIGINT, NOT NULL, REFERENCES `users`), `created_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()).\n  - **Database Constraints**:\n    - `PRIMARY KEY (blocker_id, blocked_id)`: Ensures that a user can only block another specific user once.\n  - **Database Indexes**:\n    - `idx_user_blocks_blocked_id`: Index on `blocked_id` for efficient lookups of who a user has blocked.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/migrations/000004_create_conversations_and_participants_tables.up.sql": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/migrations/000004_create_conversations_and_participants_tables.up.sql`\n- High-Level Purpose: SQL script to create the `conversations` and `conversation_participants` tables, define a custom `conversation_type` ENUM, and add an index.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Database Types**:\n    - `conversation_type`: An ENUM type with values 'private', 'group'.\n  - **Database Tables**:\n    - `conversations`: Table to store chat conversation metadata.\n      - Fields: `id` (BIGSERIAL, PRIMARY KEY), `type` (conversation_type, NOT NULL), `created_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()).\n    - `conversation_participants`: Junction table to link users to conversations.\n      - Fields: `conversation_id` (BIGINT, NOT NULL, REFERENCES `conversations`), `user_id` (BIGINT, NOT NULL, REFERENCES `users`), `joined_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()).\n  - **Database Constraints**:\n    - `PRIMARY KEY (conversation_id, user_id)`: Ensures uniqueness for each participant in a conversation.\n  - **Database Indexes**:\n    - `idx_conversation_participants_user_id`: Index on `user_id` for efficient lookups of conversations a user is part of.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/migrations/000005_create_messages_table.up.sql": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/migrations/000005_create_messages_table.up.sql`\n- High-Level Purpose: SQL script to create the `messages` table, define a custom `message_type` ENUM, and add indexes for efficient querying.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Database Types**:\n    - `message_type`: An ENUM type with values 'text', 'media'.\n  - **Database Tables**:\n    - `messages`: Table to store chat message information.\n      - Fields: `id` (BIGSERIAL, PRIMARY KEY), `conversation_id` (BIGINT, NOT NULL, REFERENCES `conversations`), `sender_id` (BIGINT, NOT NULL, REFERENCES `users`), `type` (message_type, NOT NULL, DEFAULT 'text'), `content` (TEXT, NOT NULL), `created_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()).\n  - **Database Indexes**:\n    - `idx_messages_conversation_id_created_at`: Index on `conversation_id` and `created_at` (descending) for efficient retrieval of messages in a conversation.\n    - `idx_messages_conversation_id_id`: Index on `conversation_id` and `id` (descending) for cursor-based pagination.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/config/config.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/config/config.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Handles loading and parsing application configuration from environment variables, with support for `.env` files and default values.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `Config`: Holds all application configuration parameters.\n      - Fields: `Port` (int), `DatabaseURL` (string), `RedisAddress` (string), `JWTSecretKey` (string), `AccessTokenExpiry` (time.Duration), `RefreshTokenExpiry` (time.Duration).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `Load() (*Config, error)`: Public function that loads configuration from environment variables (and `.env` file if present), parses them, and returns a `Config` struct.\n    - `getEnv(key, fallback string) string`: Internal helper function to retrieve an environment variable or return a fallback value.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/logger/logger.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/logger/logger.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides a utility function to create a structured logger using Go's `slog` package.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `New(w io.Writer) *slog.Logger`: Public function that creates and returns a new `slog.Logger` instance. It configures the logger to use a JSON handler and sets the default logging level to `LevelDebug`.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/middleware/auth.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/middleware/auth.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides an HTTP middleware function to authenticate requests using JWT tokens, extracting the user ID and adding it to the request context.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `Auth(jwtSecret string) func(http.Handler) http.Handler`: Public function that returns an `http.Handler` middleware. It extracts a JWT token from either the `Authorization` header (Bearer token) or a `auth` query parameter (for WebSockets), validates it, and if valid, adds the `UserID` from the claims to the request context.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - HTTP Middleware: Implements the standard `http.Handler` interface for chaining request processing.\n  - JWT Authentication: Uses `util.ValidateToken` to verify the token's signature and claims.\n  - Token Extraction: Supports extracting tokens from both `Authorization` headers and URL query parameters.\n  - Context Enrichment: Adds the authenticated `user_id` to the request context for downstream handlers.\n  - Error Handling: Returns `401 Unauthorized` for missing or invalid tokens.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/middleware/logger.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/middleware/logger.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides an HTTP middleware function to log details of incoming requests.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `RequestLogger(next http.Handler) http.Handler`: Public function that returns an `http.Handler` middleware. It logs the HTTP method, path, duration, and remote address for each request before passing it to the next handler.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - HTTP Middleware: Implements the standard `http.Handler` interface for chaining request processing.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/util/hash.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/util/hash.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides utility functions for securely hashing passwords and comparing plain text passwords against hashes using bcrypt.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `HashPassword(password string) (string, error)`: Public function that takes a plain text password and returns its bcrypt hash.\n    - `CheckPasswordHash(password, hash string) bool`: Public function that compares a plain text password with a bcrypt hash, returning `true` if they match, `false` otherwise.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/util/token.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/util/token.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides utility functions for generating and validating JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) with custom claims.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `JWTClaims`: Custom claims structure for JWTs, embedding `jwt.RegisteredClaims`.\n      - Fields: `UserID` (int64), `jwt.RegisteredClaims`.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `GenerateToken(userID int64, expiry time.Duration, secretKey string) (string, error)`: Public function that creates a new JWT for a given user ID, expiry duration, and secret key.\n    - `ValidateToken(tokenString string, secretKey string) (*JWTClaims, error)`: Public function that parses and validates a JWT string using the provided secret key. Returns the `JWTClaims` if valid, or an error otherwise.\n",
