  "quikchat-frontend/public/index.html": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/public/index.html`\n- High-Level Purpose: The main HTML file that serves as the entry point for the QuikChat frontend application, defining the basic page structure and loading necessary resources.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - This is an HTML file and does not contain code definitions.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Single Page Application (SPA) Structure: Contains a root `div` (`#app`) where JavaScript components will be rendered.\n  - Resource Loading: Links to the compiled Tailwind CSS and imports the main JavaScript module (`src/index.js`).\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/api/auth.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/api/auth.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides functions to interact with the backend's authentication API endpoints for user registration and login.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `API_BASE_URL`: Module-level constant defining the base URL for API requests.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `handleResponse(response)`: Internal helper function that checks if an HTTP response is OK, parses the JSON, and throws an error if the response status is not successful.\n    - `register(username, password)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a POST request to the `/auth/register` endpoint with user credentials.\n    - `login(username, password)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a POST request to the `/auth/login` endpoint with user credentials.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/api/friends.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/api/friends.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides asynchronous functions to interact with the backend API for managing friend relationships and requests.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `API_BASE_URL`: Module-level constant defining the base URL for API requests.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `listFriends()`: Public asynchronous function that fetches the current user's list of friends.\n    - `listIncomingRequests()`: Public asynchronous function that fetches pending friend requests sent to the current user.\n    - `sendFriendRequest(username)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a friend request to a specified username.\n    - `respondToRequest(requestID, action)`: Public asynchronous function that responds to a friend request (accept or decline) by its ID.\n    - `unfriend(username)`: Public asynchronous function that removes a friend by their username.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - API Client: Encapsulates `fetch` calls to specific friend-related endpoints.\n  - Authentication: Uses `getAccessToken()` to include a Bearer token in request headers for authorization.\n  - Error Handling: Leverages `handleResponse` (imported from `auth.js`) for consistent API response processing.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/api/messages.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/api/messages.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides asynchronous functions to interact with the backend API for sending, fetching messages, and managing media uploads.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `API_BASE_URL`: Module-level constant defining the base URL for API requests.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `fetchMessages(conversationId, cursor = null)`: Public asynchronous function that fetches a list of messages for a given conversation, supporting cursor-based pagination.\n    - `sendMessage(conversationId, message)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a new message (text or media) to a specified conversation.\n    - `getPresignedUrl(filename)`: Public asynchronous function that requests a presigned URL from the backend for uploading a file.\n    - `uploadFile(uploadUrl, file)`: Public asynchronous function that uploads a file directly to a given presigned URL (e.g., S3).\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - API Client: Encapsulates `fetch` calls to specific message-related endpoints.\n  - Authentication: Uses `getAccessToken()` to include a Bearer token in request headers for authorization.\n  - Error Handling: Leverages `handleResponse` (imported from `auth.js`) for consistent API response processing.\n  - Media Upload: Separates getting a presigned URL from the actual file upload.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/api/users.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/api/users.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides asynchronous functions to interact with the backend API for user profile management and blocking.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `API_BASE_URL`: Module-level constant defining the base URL for API requests.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `getProfile(username)`: Public asynchronous function that fetches a user's profile by username.\n    - `updateProfile(profileData)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a PUT request to update the current user's profile.\n    - `blockUser(username)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a POST request to block a specified user.\n    - `unblockUser(username)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a DELETE request to unblock a specified user.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - API Client: Encapsulates `fetch` calls to specific user-related endpoints.\n  - Authentication: Uses `getAccessToken()` to include a Bearer token in request headers for authorization.\n  - Error Handling: Leverages `handleResponse` (imported from `auth.js`) for consistent API response processing.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/components/MessageDisplay.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/components/MessageDisplay.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Renders a single chat message component, displaying its content, sender, and timestamp, with different styling for own messages.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `MessageDisplay({ message, isOwnMessage })`: Public function that returns a DOM element representing a single message. It dynamically applies CSS classes based on whether the message was sent by the current user.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Single Page Application (SPA) Component: Dynamically creates and styles a DOM element.\n  - Conditional Rendering/Styling: Adjusts layout and colors based on the `isOwnMessage` prop.\n  - Data Display: Formats and displays message content, sender name, and timestamp.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/components/Navbar.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/components/Navbar.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Renders a reusable navigation bar component for the QuikChat frontend, providing links to different application pages.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `Navbar()`: Public function that returns a DOM `nav` element containing the application title and navigation links.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Single Page Application (SPA) Component: Dynamically creates and styles a navigation bar using Tailwind CSS classes.\n  - Client-side Navigation: Uses hash-based `href` attributes for internal SPA routing.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/index.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/index.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: The main entry point for the QuikChat frontend application, responsible for client-side routing, authentication checks, and initializing global services.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `routes`: Object mapping hash paths to page components.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `router()`: Internal function that determines the current route based on `window.location.hash`, checks authentication status, renders the appropriate page, and manages WebSocket connection/disconnection.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Client-side Routing: Implements a simple hash-based router.\n  - Authentication Gate: Redirects to the login page if not authenticated, or to the chat page if authenticated and trying to access login.\n  - WebSocket Integration: Connects `WebSocketService` on authentication and disconnects on logout or unauthentication.\n  - Global Event Listeners: Attaches `router` to `DOMContentLoaded` and `hashchange` events.\n  - Custom Event Handling: Listens for a custom `logout` event to clear authentication and redirect.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/pages/ChatPage.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/pages/ChatPage.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Renders the main chat interface, including message display, input form, and handles real-time message updates via WebSocket.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `CURRENT_USER_ID`: Hardcoded user ID for demonstration.\n    - `CONVERSATION_ID`: Hardcoded conversation ID for demonstration.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `ChatPage()`: Public function that returns a DOM element representing the chat page. It initializes the UI, fetches initial messages, handles sending text and media messages, and integrates with the `chatStore` and `WebSocketService` for real-time updates.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Single Page Application (SPA) Component: Dynamically creates and manipulates DOM elements to build the chat UI.\n  - UI State Management: Uses `chatStore` to manage and render messages, subscribing to changes.\n  - API Interaction: Calls `fetchMessages`, `sendMessage`, `getPresignedUrl`, `uploadFile` from `messages.js`.\n  - WebSocket Integration: Uses `WebSocketService` to listen for incoming real-time messages.\n  - Infinite Scrolling: Implements logic to load older messages when the user scrolls to the top of the message area.\n  - Event Handling: Attaches event listeners for form submission and file input changes.\n  - Media Upload: Provides a file input and button for uploading media, using presigned URLs.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/pages/FriendsPage.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/pages/FriendsPage.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Renders the user interface for managing friends and friend requests, displaying incoming requests and the current friends list.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `FriendsPage()`: Public function that returns a DOM element representing the friends and requests page. It fetches and displays incoming friend requests and the user's friends list, providing buttons to accept or decline requests.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Single Page Application (SPA) Component: Dynamically creates and manipulates DOM elements to build the page.\n  - UI State Management: Displays \"Loading...\" and then populates lists based on API responses.\n  - API Interaction: Calls `listFriends`, `listIncomingRequests`, and `respondToRequest` from `friends.js`.\n  - Event Handling: Attaches `onclick` handlers to accept/decline buttons to interact with the API and update the UI.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/pages/LoginPage.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/pages/LoginPage.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Renders the login and registration forms, handles user input, interacts with the authentication API, and manages local authentication state.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `LoginPage()`: Public function that returns a DOM element representing the login/registration page. It sets up event listeners for form submission (login and register) and a toggle link to switch between the two forms. It calls `login` or `register` API functions and `setTokens` on success.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Single Page Application (SPA) Component: Returns a dynamically created DOM element.\n  - Form Handling: Manages form input and submission for both login and registration.\n  - UI State Management: Toggles visibility and text content based on `isLogin` state.\n  - API Interaction: Calls `login` and `register` functions from `auth.js`.\n  - Client-side Routing: Redirects to '/' on successful authentication.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/pages/ProfilePage.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/pages/ProfilePage.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Renders a user's profile page, displaying their username, display name, join date, and placeholder action buttons.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `ProfilePage()`: Public function that returns a DOM element representing the user profile page. It fetches profile data (currently hardcoded to 'me' or 'testuser' for simplicity) and displays it, along with placeholder buttons for actions like \"Edit Profile\", \"Add Friend\", and \"Block User\".\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Single Page Application (SPA) Component: Dynamically creates and styles DOM elements.\n  - API Interaction: Calls `getProfile` from `users.js` to fetch user data.\n  - Placeholder Functionality: Buttons are present but do not yet have full functionality implemented.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/services/WebSocketService.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/services/WebSocketService.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Manages the WebSocket connection for the frontend application, handling connection, disconnection, message reception, and reconnection logic.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Variables**:\n    - `socket`: Module-level variable to hold the `WebSocket` instance.\n    - `messageListeners`: Array to store callback functions for incoming messages.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `connect()`: Public function that establishes a WebSocket connection, including authentication via a query parameter. Handles `onopen`, `onmessage`, `onclose`, and `onerror` events, with a reconnection mechanism.\n    - `disconnect()`: Public function that gracefully closes the WebSocket connection and prevents automatic reconnection.\n    - `addMessageListener(callback)`: Public function to register a callback for incoming WebSocket messages.\n    - `removeMessageListener(callback)`: Public function to unregister a message callback.\n  - **Exports**:\n    - `WebSocketService`: An object exposing `connect`, `disconnect`, `addMessageListener`, `removeMessageListener`.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Singleton Service: Manages a single WebSocket connection for the application.\n  - Event Listener Pattern: Allows multiple components to subscribe to incoming WebSocket messages.\n  - Reconnection Logic: Automatically attempts to reconnect after a connection is closed or an error occurs.\n  - Authentication: Passes the access token as a query parameter during WebSocket handshake.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/store/authStore.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/store/authStore.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Manages the storage and retrieval of authentication tokens (access and refresh tokens) using browser's `localStorage`.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `ACCESS_TOKEN_KEY`: String constant for the access token key in local storage.\n    - `REFRESH_TOKEN_KEY`: String constant for the refresh token key in local storage.\n  - **Variables**:\n    - `accessToken`: Module-level variable storing the current access token, initialized from local storage.\n    - `refreshToken`: Module-level variable storing the current refresh token, initialized from local storage.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `setTokens(newAccessToken, newRefreshToken)`: Public function that updates the `accessToken` and `refreshToken` variables and persists them to `localStorage`.\n    - `getAccessToken()`: Public function that returns the current `accessToken`.\n    - `getRefreshToken()`: Public function that returns the current `refreshToken`.\n    - `logout()`: Public function that clears the `accessToken` and `refreshToken` variables and removes them from `localStorage`.\n    - `isAuthenticated()`: Public function that returns `true` if an `accessToken` is present, indicating a user is logged in.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Client-side State Management: Uses module-level variables and `localStorage` for simple authentication state.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/store/chatStore.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/store/chatStore.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides a simple, in-memory state management solution for chat conversations and messages in the frontend.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Variables**:\n    - `state`: Module-level object holding the current chat state (conversations, messages, active conversation ID).\n    - `listeners`: Array to store functions subscribed to state changes.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `subscribe(listener)`: Public function to add a listener that will be called when the state changes. Returns an `unsubscribe` function.\n    - `notify()`: Internal function to call all registered listeners.\n    - `addMessage(conversationId, message)`: Public function to add a new message to a specific conversation, preventing duplicates.\n    - `prependMessages(conversationId, messages)`: Public function to add messages to the beginning of a conversation's message list (e.g., for loading older messages).\n    - `setActiveConversation(conversationId)`: Public function to set the currently active conversation.\n    - `getState()`: Public function to retrieve the current state object.\n  - **Exports**:\n    - `chatStore`: An object exposing the public state management functions.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Simple State Management: Uses a basic publish-subscribe pattern.\n  - In-memory Store: Stores application state directly in JavaScript memory.\n  - Immutability (partial): Updates state by creating new arrays for messages to trigger reactivity.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/styles/input.css": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/styles/input.css`\n- High-Level Purpose: Serves as the main entry point for Tailwind CSS, importing its base, component, and utility styles.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - This is a CSS file and does not contain code definitions.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Tailwind CSS Directives: Uses `@tailwind` directives to inject Tailwind's pre-generated styles.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/types/types.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/types/types.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines JSDoc type definitions for common data structures used in the QuikChat frontend, such as `User` and `Message`.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Types**:\n    - `User`: JSDoc typedef for a user object.\n      - Properties: `id` (number), `username` (string), `display_name` (string), `profile_image_url` (string|null), `created_at` (string), `updated_at` (string), `last_seen_at` (string|null).\n    - `Message`: JSDoc typedef for a message object.\n      - Properties: `id` (number), `conversation_id` (number), `sender_id` (number), `type` ('text' | 'media'), `content` (string), `created_at` (string), `sender` (User, optional).\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - JSDoc Type Definitions: Provides type hints for JavaScript code, improving readability and tooling support without requiring TypeScript compilation.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/utils/dom.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/utils/dom.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides a utility function to render a given component into the main application root element.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `appElement`: Module-level constant referencing the DOM element with `id=\"app\"`.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `render(component)`: Public function that clears the content of the `#app` element and appends the result of calling the provided `component` function.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/tailwind.config.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/tailwind.config.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Configures Tailwind CSS for the frontend project, specifying which files to scan for Tailwind classes.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - This is a configuration file and does not contain code definitions.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Tailwind CSS Configuration: Defines `content` paths for JIT mode to scan HTML and JavaScript files for class names.\n"
